d-release oxcarbazepine 2400 mg/day 14.2%; Barcs2000 oxcarbazepine 2400 mg/day 42%; Glauser2000 oxcarbazepine 30-46 mg/kg/day 26%)","rationale":"French and Barcs calculations are correct. Glauser2000 adds an in-range median-percent-change differential of 26%.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/"]},{"current_value":"8.1 % (drug minus placebo seizure-freedom differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: French2013 extended-release oxcarbazepine 2400 mg/day 8.1%)","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"French2013 reports seizure-free rates of 11.4% for 2400 mg/day SPN-804 and 3.3% for placebo, a differential of 8.1%; Barcs2000 and Glauser2000 abstracts do not provide seizure-freedom percentages.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/"]},{"current_value":"French2013|12.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/|366; Barcs2000|37|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/|694","field":"plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"French2013|12.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/|366; Barcs2000|37|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/|694; Glauser2000|19|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/|267","rationale":"Existing plot values match cited abstracts; add Glauser2000 because it is a qualifying placebo-controlled RCT with extractable RR50 differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/"]},{"current_value":"French2013|14.2|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/|366; Barcs2000|42|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/|694","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"French2013|14.2|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/|366; Barcs2000|42|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/|694; Glauser2000|26|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/|267","rationale":"Existing plot values match cited abstracts; add Glauser2000 because it is a qualifying placebo-controlled RCT with extractable median-percent-change differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/"]},{"current_value":"French2013|8.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/|366","field":"plot_diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"No change.","rationale":"French2013 supports the 8.1% seizure-freedom differential; no other retained abstract provides a seizure-freedom differential.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66; published=Nov 17, 2025; title=OXTELLAR XR (OXCARBAZEPINE) TABLET [SUPERNUS PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66; effective_time=20251022; title=OXTELLAR XR / OXCARBAZEPINE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for FDA boxed-warning verification; use FDA/openFDA metadata instead.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","reason":"Substantive no-boxed-warning conclusion is supportable, but the source wording must be FDA/openFDA, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"NCBI LiverTox anticonvulsants table; Epilepsy Society ASM list; Epilepsy Foundation Australia ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; NCBI LiverTox; NCBI StatPearls; PubMed RCT abstracts; ClinicalTrials.gov","reason":"Replace non-trusted and DailyMed source wording with the trusted sources actually used for row facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/021014s050lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548414/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK482313/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00772603"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata labeling","reason":"The mechanism facts are supported by FDA labeling; avoid DailyMed wording under the trusted-source policy.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/021014s050lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"OXC; OXC XR; SPN-804; TRI476","reason":"Adds trial and PubMed aliases without treating them as alternate generic names.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00772603","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00975715"]},{"current_value":"French2013|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/; Barcs2000|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/; Schachter1999b|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10599816/; Schachter1999|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10078718/; Cramer1999|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10599817/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"French2013|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/; Barcs2000|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/; Schachter1999|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10078718/; Glauser2000|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/","reason":"Adds a missed randomized placebo-controlled pediatric adjunctive RCT and removes two comment/letter records that are not independent primary trial reports.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10078718/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 37/65 on 2026-05-15: 5 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 24 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Audit on 2026-05-20: French2013, Barcs2000, Schachter1999, and Glauser2000 are qualifying placebo-controlled randomized oxcarbazepine seizure trial reports. Schachter1999b (PMID 10599816) and Cramer1999 (PMID 10599817) are comment/letter records on the Schachter monotherapy trial and should not be counted as independent RCT reports. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values from French2013, Barcs2000, and Glauser2000; Schachter1999 reports exit/time-to-event outcomes but not extractable RR50, MPC, or seizure-freedom percentages.","reason":"Updates RCT verification notes to match PubMed evidence.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10078718/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10881246/"]},{"current_value":"Calcium channel / alpha-2-delta; Potassium channel","field":"filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"Sodium channel; Potassium channel; Calcium channel","reason":"FDA labeling supports sodium-channel blockade and possible potassium/high-voltage calcium effects, not alpha-2-delta.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/021014s050lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver/hepatic; Renal/no major metabolism","field":"filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver/hepatic; Renal excretion","reason":"Oxcarbazepine is extensively metabolized; renal excretion is of metabolites.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/021014s050lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"French2013","pmid":"24359313","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PMID, drug, Phase 3 randomized double-blind parallel-group design, placebo comparator, and partial-onset seizure population are verified.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24359313/"},{"label":"Barcs2000","pmid":"11114219","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PMID, oxcarbazepine assignment, randomized double-blind placebo-controlled four-arm adjunctive design, and partial-seizure population are verified. PubMed does not tag phase, but this is a qualifying dose-ranging controlled trial used for efficacy/outcomes.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11114219/"},{"label":"Schachter1999b","pmid":"10599816","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links or move to notes; requires user approval because it removes an existing link.","rationale":"PubMed lists this as a comment/letter on the Schachter monotherapy trial with no abstract, not an independent phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT report.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10599816/"},{"label":"Schachter1999","pmid":"10078718","proposed_action":"Keep, but do not use for RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom plots unless full-text extractable percentages are added.","rationale":"PMID, oxcarbazepine, randomized double-blind placebo-control monotherapy design, and partial-seizure population are verified; abstract reports time-to-exit and seizure-frequency significance, not extractable RR50/MPC/seizure-freedom percentages.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10078718/"},{"label":"Cramer1999","pmid":"10599817","proposed_action":"Remove from pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links or move to notes; requires user approval because it removes an existing link.","rationale":"PubMed lists this as a comment/letter on the Schachter monotherapy trial with no abstract, not an independent phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT report.","status":"not_phase_ii_iii","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10599817/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66; published=Nov 17, 2025; title=OXTELLAR XR (OXCARBAZEPINE) TABLET [SUPERNUS PHARMACEUTICALS, INC.]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66; effective_time=20251022; title=OXTELLAR XR / OXCARBAZEPINE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%22aa610e56-1d1d-11e1-8bc2-0800200c9a66%22&limit=5","reason":"Black-box-warning verification must use FDA/openFDA, FDA labels, or Drugs@FDA, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://